 "name": "Programming, broadcasting, news agency and other content distribution activities",
 "section": "J",
 "summary": "Broadcasters and streaming services write about AI in content discovery and recommendation, ad targeting and addressable advertising, dubbing, subtitling and production workflows, and about synthetic media, deepfakes and performer rights. Social networks and other content platforms are both heavy AI users and AI builders: ranking algorithms, AI content moderation, generative creator tools, AI advertising automation and the compute capex behind them, under platform regulation (DSA, Online Safety Act) and disputes over training on user and news content. News agencies focus on verification, licensing of archives to AI developers and automated reporting.",
